<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:zeebe="http://camunda.org/schema/zeebe/1.0" id="Defs_session_craft" targetNamespace="http://graph-agent/bpmn">
  <bpmn:process id="session_craft" name="Agent session (craft-first)" isExecutable="true">
    <bpmn:documentation>The vision's own sentence, as one graph: start with a prompt, hand it to
craft_graph to interpret and build the steps that follow, then run those
steps -- with the simple case reproducing Pi's own loop.

The first lap goes straight from the prompt into craft; only a later lap
asks for a fresh intent through a form first, and "more work?" is decided
right there before looping back into craft -- not after a whole crafted lap
has already run on a prompt nobody wanted acted on (issue #72: ticking "End
the session instead" used to still cost one full craft lap, including a
billed model turn, because the only place that read session_done sat after
craft, not before it). When craft has nothing to add (rejected, or
exhausted its redraft attempts), this falls back to pi_default_loop rather
than ending having done nothing -- so the vision's "start simple ... allow
iterating to more dedicated definitions" is one graph, not two.

The definitions id must stay stable for the life of the session: recovery
matches a snapshot to a graph on that id.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:extensionElements>
      <zeebe:userTaskForm id="session_craft_intent_form">{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/@bpmn-io/form-js@1/dist/assets/form-json-schema/schema.json",
  "components": [
    {
      "label": "Goal",
      "type": "textarea",
      "key": "intent",
      "id": "intent"
    },
    {
      "label": "Context or constraints",
      "type": "textarea",
      "key": "context",
      "id": "context"
    },
    {
      "label": "End the session instead",
      "type": "checkbox",
      "key": "done",
      "id": "done"
    }
  ],
  "type": "default",
  "id": "session_craft_intent_form",
  "schemaVersion": 18
}</zeebe:userTaskForm>
    </bpmn:extensionElements>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="session_craft_start" name="Session start">
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_craft</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_craft" sourceRef="session_craft_start" targetRef="gw_craft_entry" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_craft_entry" name="Enter craft">
      <bpmn:documentation>A plain merge of the two ways this lap reaches craft -- a fresh session
start, or looping back after "more work?" -- explicit rather than the
two-way implicit merge bpmnlint's fake-join rule used to only warn about
(now an error). A plain activity with more than one incoming edge does not
join at all in this engine, it just runs again per arrival, which is
exactly the behaviour this gateway keeps.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>to_craft</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>continue</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>into_craft</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="into_craft" sourceRef="gw_craft_entry" targetRef="craft" />
    <bpmn:callActivity id="craft" name="Craft an extension" calledElement="craft_graph">
      <bpmn:documentation>Calls the crafting graph, which is spliced into this definition when the
session is created -- bpmn-elements resolves calledElement within the same
definition, and keeping it inline makes the session one self-contained,
self-documenting artifact.

The first lap's intent is unset, so draft_fragment's own
"=if intent = null then prompt else intent" reads the prompt runSession
seeds directly -- no gate needed before this first call.

The zeebe:output below is required, not cosmetic: gw_crafted routes on
extend_status, which craft_graph's own apply_extension sets deep inside a
*different* linked process. engine.ts never bridges a callActivity's own
child-process variables into the caller's scope for gateway conditions the
way it does for a harness's zeebe:ioMapping (sharedOutput) -- a gateway
condition is evaluated natively by bpmn-elements against this process's own
environment only. Without this output mapping, extend_status is simply
never a variable here at all, and gw_crafted's condition always warns
"not found" and falls through to its default (fallback_default), even right
after a successful apply (real Haiku repro, issue #66: apply_extension
splices fine, but gw_crafted still takes the "nothing crafted" branch into
run_default -- which the *next* graph:extend-triggered stop/resume cycle
then tries to resume a second time, throwing "cannot resume running
process pi_default_loop"). "=extend_status" reads bare, the same as any
other zeebe:output source -- see engine.ts's applyUnharnessedOutput for why
a callActivity's own signaled output needs unwrapping first to make that
true.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:output source="=extend_status" target="extend_status" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>into_craft</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>craft_to_route</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="craft_to_route" sourceRef="craft" targetRef="gw_crafted" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_crafted" name="Something crafted?" default="fallback_default">
      <bpmn:documentation>extend_status is only ever "success" for the lap that just spliced
something in -- draft_fragment resets it to null on every entry into
craft_graph, so a rejected or exhausted lap never inherits a stale value
from an earlier successful one.

The "crafted_ok" flow below is the single obvious place a splice lands:
graph:extend rewires its target from gw_more into whatever it added, the
same way session-skeleton's own craft -&gt; gw_more edge works.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>craft_to_route</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>crafted_ok</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>fallback_default</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="crafted_ok" name="crafted" sourceRef="gw_crafted" targetRef="gw_craft_done">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=extend_status = "success"</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="fallback_default" name="nothing crafted" sourceRef="gw_crafted" targetRef="run_default" />
    <bpmn:callActivity id="run_default" name="Run the default Pi loop" calledElement="pi_default_loop">
      <bpmn:documentation>Degrades to session-default's own behaviour when craft rejected the
extension or gave up redrafting it, so a lap with nothing crafted still does
the work the prompt or intent asked for instead of ending empty.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>fallback_default</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>default_done</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="default_done" sourceRef="run_default" targetRef="gw_craft_done" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_craft_done" name="Lap done">
      <bpmn:documentation>A plain join, kept separate from gw_more's own fork -- a single gateway
that both joins and forks is ambiguous BPMN (bpmnlint's
no-gateway-join-fork) even though bpmn-elements would run it.

Routes straight to await_intent, not through a "more work?" decision first
(issue #72): session_done is only known once await_intent's form is
answered, so asking "more work?" here, before that form even exists yet on
the first lap, would need session_done to already be set -- it is not, so
the only place that can honestly decide whether to loop back into craft is
after the form, not before it.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>crafted_ok</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>default_done</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_await_intent</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_await_intent" sourceRef="gw_craft_done" targetRef="await_intent" />
    <bpmn:userTask id="await_intent" name="What should the agent do next?">
      <bpmn:extensionElements>
        <zeebe:userTask />
        <zeebe:formDefinition formId="session_craft_intent_form" />
        <zeebe:ioMapping>
          <zeebe:output source="=intent" target="intent" />
          <zeebe:output source="=context" target="context" />
          <zeebe:output source="=done" target="session_done" />
        </zeebe:ioMapping>
      </bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>to_await_intent</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>to_gw_more</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:userTask>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="to_gw_more" sourceRef="await_intent" targetRef="gw_more" />
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="gw_more" name="More work?" default="continue">
      <bpmn:documentation>Checked immediately after await_intent's own form, before craft ever runs
again -- not after a whole crafted lap, the way an earlier version of this
graph had it (issue #72). Ticking "End the session instead" now ends the
session without another draft_fragment turn being billed on a prompt
nobody wanted acted on.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>to_gw_more</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>continue</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>session_over</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="continue" name="continue" sourceRef="gw_more" targetRef="gw_craft_entry" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="session_over" name="done" sourceRef="gw_more" targetRef="session_craft_end">
      <bpmn:conditionExpression xsi:type="bpmn:tFormalExpression">=session_done = true</bpmn:conditionExpression>
    </bpmn:sequenceFlow>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="session_craft_end" name="Session ended">
      <bpmn:incoming>session_over</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_session_craft">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_session_craft" bpmnElement="session_craft">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="session_craft_start_di" bpmnElement="session_craft_start">
        <dc:Bounds x="57" y="52" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_craft_entry_di" bpmnElement="gw_craft_entry" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="200" y="45" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="craft_di" bpmnElement="craft">
        <dc:Bounds x="325" y="30" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_crafted_di" bpmnElement="gw_crafted" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="500" y="45" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_craft_done_di" bpmnElement="gw_craft_done" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="800" y="45" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="await_intent_di" bpmnElement="await_intent">
        <dc:Bounds x="925" y="30" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="gw_more_di" bpmnElement="gw_more" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="1100" y="45" width="50" height="50" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="session_craft_end_di" bpmnElement="session_craft_end">
        <dc:Bounds x="1257" y="52" width="36" height="36" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="run_default_di" bpmnElement="run_default">
        <dc:Bounds x="625" y="170" width="100" height="80" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_craft_di" bpmnElement="to_craft">
        <di:waypoint x="93" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="200" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="into_craft_di" bpmnElement="into_craft">
        <di:waypoint x="250" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="325" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="craft_to_route_di" bpmnElement="craft_to_route">
        <di:waypoint x="425" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="500" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="crafted_ok_di" bpmnElement="crafted_ok">
        <di:waypoint x="550" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="800" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="fallback_default_di" bpmnElement="fallback_default">
        <di:waypoint x="525" y="95" />
        <di:waypoint x="525" y="210" />
        <di:waypoint x="625" y="210" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_await_intent_di" bpmnElement="to_await_intent">
        <di:waypoint x="850" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="925" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="to_gw_more_di" bpmnElement="to_gw_more">
        <di:waypoint x="1025" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="1100" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="continue_di" bpmnElement="continue">
        <di:waypoint x="1125" y="95" />
        <di:waypoint x="1125" y="140" />
        <di:waypoint x="225" y="140" />
        <di:waypoint x="225" y="95" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="session_over_di" bpmnElement="session_over">
        <di:waypoint x="1150" y="70" />
        <di:waypoint x="1257" y="70" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="default_done_di" bpmnElement="default_done">
        <di:waypoint x="725" y="210" />
        <di:waypoint x="825" y="210" />
        <di:waypoint x="825" y="95" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
